module System/Numerics

# Narrowing conversions that do not fail: `x.to_wrap[U8]()` keeps the low bits of the value, and `x.to_clamp[U8]()`
# gives the nearest value the target holds. `x.to[U8]()` is the conversion that crashes when the value does not fit.

### Converts to `U8` keeping the low 8 bits: a value outside the `U8` range wraps around.
### :returns: The low 8 bits of this value as a `U8`.
@rv("S8.to_wrap")
routine S8.to_wrap[U8]() -> U8

### Converts to `U8`, giving the nearest `U8` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `U8`'s bound on the side it lies past.
@rv("S8.to_clamp")
routine S8.to_clamp[U8]() -> U8

### Converts to `U16` keeping the low 16 bits: a value outside the `U16` range wraps around.
### :returns: The low 16 bits of this value as a `U16`.
@rv("S8.to_wrap")
routine S8.to_wrap[U16]() -> U16

### Converts to `U16`, giving the nearest `U16` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `U16`'s bound on the side it lies past.
@rv("S8.to_clamp")
routine S8.to_clamp[U16]() -> U16

### Converts to `U32` keeping the low 32 bits: a value outside the `U32` range wraps around.
### :returns: The low 32 bits of this value as a `U32`.
@rv("S8.to_wrap")
routine S8.to_wrap[U32]() -> U32

### Converts to `U32`, giving the nearest `U32` when this value is outside its range.
### :returns: This value, or `U32`'s bound on the side it lies past.
@rv("S8.to_clamp")
routine S8.to_clamp[U32]() -> U32

### Converts to `U64` keeping the low 64 bits: a value outside the `U64` range wraps around.
